window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b64a9457088d1171"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"image-inputs\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">图像输入</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>当任务依赖视觉上下文时，例如错误截图、界面设计、架构图或已有素材，可以将图像添加到提示词中。说明希望 ChatGPT 检查什么以及想要得到什么结果；不要只依赖图像来传达任务。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在按住 <kbd>Shift</kbd> 的同时，将图像拖入提示词编辑框即可将其作为上下文。你也可以让 ChatGPT 检查系统中的图像，或使用截图工具在其他应用中验证工作。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT 网页版编辑框中附加、粘贴或拖入图像。在提示词中告诉 ChatGPT 要检查什么，以及希望得到什么结果。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>将图像粘贴到交互式编辑框中，或在命令行中传入一个或多个文件：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex -i screenshot.png \"Explain this error and suggest the smallest fix\"\ncodex --image before.png,after.png \"Compare these states and list the regressions\"\n</code></pre> <p>对于多张图像，请用逗号分隔路径，或重复使用 <code>--image</code>。Codex 接受常见的图像格式，包括 PNG 和 JPEG。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在按住 <kbd>Shift</kbd> 的同时，将图像拖入提示词编辑框，这样扩展就会接受拖放，而不是将图像传给编辑器。</p> <p><a id=\"write-the-prompt-around-the-image\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">围绕图像编写提示词</h2> <p>说明图像展示的内容，指出关键区域，并说明输出和约束。如果附加多张图像，请标明每张图像，并解释希望 ChatGPT 如何比较它们。</p> <p>例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare this checkout screen with the design. Fix spacing and typography only;\ndo not change behavior. Verify the result with a new screenshot.\n</code></pre> <p>中文意思：请将此结账界面与设计稿进行比较；只调整间距和文字排版，不要改变原有行为。请使用一张新截图验证结果。</p> <p><a id=\"use-the-right-image-feature\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">使用合适的图像功能</h2> <p>当你希望 ChatGPT 检查视觉参考时，使用图像输入。当你希望 ChatGPT 创建或编辑图像时，使用<a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图像生成</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"image-inputs\">Image inputs</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Add images to a prompt when the task depends on visual context, such as an error screenshot, interface design, architecture diagram, or existing asset. Explain what ChatGPT should inspect and what outcome you want; don't rely on the image alone to communicate the task.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Drag an image into the prompt composer while holding <kbd>Shift</kbd> to include it as context. You can also ask ChatGPT to inspect an image on your system or use a screenshot tool to verify work in another app.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Attach, paste, or drag an image into the ChatGPT web composer. In the prompt, tell ChatGPT what to inspect and what result you want from the image.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Paste an image into the interactive composer, or pass one or more files on the command line:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex -i screenshot.png \"Explain this error and suggest the smallest fix\"\ncodex --image before.png,after.png \"Compare these states and list the regressions\"\n</code></pre> <p>For multiple images, separate paths with commas or repeat <code>--image</code>. Codex accepts common image formats, including PNG and JPEG.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Drag an image into the prompt composer while holding <kbd>Shift</kbd> so the extension accepts the drop instead of passing it to the editor.</p> <h2 id=\"write-the-prompt-around-the-image\">Write the prompt around the image</h2> <p>Name what the image shows, point to the area that matters, and state the output and constraints. If you attach more than one image, identify each one and explain how ChatGPT should compare them.</p> <p>For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare this checkout screen with the design. Fix spacing and typography only;\ndo not change behavior. Verify the result with a new screenshot.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"use-the-right-image-feature\">Use the right image feature</h2> <p>Use an image input when you want ChatGPT to inspect a visual reference. Use <a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">image generation</a> when you want ChatGPT to create or edit an image.</p>"};
